From 3d8232cd3f1bdfc291c7aae6c056fe41c3958fe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:35:26 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] MCP create_chat on a place: a sandbox of the chat's own

create_chat and create_chats take place (a sandbox provider, by id or
name) and template (by id or exact name, asked of the account each time;
none or blank is Blank), as the composer's Docker Sandbox and Template
rows do. Harness and model are checked against the template's own catalog
(place:<provider>:<template>); what it hasn't got is refused, naming what
it has. The sandbox's device and checkout come back from the engine, and
the reply says the sandbox is still being made. Not with device, cloud,
cwd or branch.
